 {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "brain"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and spinal cord. The most common presentation is sudden onset of severe novel headache. SAH from ruptured cerebral aneurysms is associated with high mortality and morbidity hence clinician’s high index of suspicion and proper initial management is crucial for patient’s survival and improved functional outcome."}]}, {"id": "body-06098", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Clinical Presentation", "runs": [{"text": "Clinical"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Presentation"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-06099", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Severe headache (worst headache of life)", "runs": [{"text": "Severe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "headache"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(worst"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "headache"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "life)"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1650"}}, {"id": "body-06100", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Altered mental status that may progress to coma", "runs": [{"text": "Altered"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "mental"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "status"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "that"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "may"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "progress"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "coma"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1650"}}, {"id": "body-06101", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Focal neurological deficits", "runs": [{"text": "Focal"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "neurological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "deficits"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1650"}}, {"id": "body-06102", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "Seizures", "runs": [{"text": "Seizures"}], "list": {"level": 0, "numberingId": "1650"}}, {"id": "body-06104", "type": "paragraph", "style": "ListParagraph", "text": "CBC, PT/PTT/INR", "runs": [{"text": "CBC,"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "PT/PTT/INR"}], "list": {"lev